  <article>
    <div class="article-header">
      <h1>Maine Cannabis POS Comparison: 2026 Vendor Side-by-Side</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Verified published pricing, Metrc integration depth, and ecommerce packaging for Flowhub, Dutchie, Cova, Treez, Jane, Meadow, and MJ Platform</p>
    </div>

    <Callout type="warning">
      <p><strong>How to use this guide.</strong> Maine cannabis retail is a YMYL ("Your Money or Your Life") decision — multi-year contracts, monthly recurring spend, and state-license compliance all depend on your POS choice. We have labeled every pricing cell in this comparison as either vendor-published (linked to the source) or quote-only. We have not constructed rankings; instead we surface verifiable differences and let you shortlist with your accountant and attorney. If you're still deciding whether you need a cannabis-specialized POS at all, start with our general <a href="/guides/maine-dispensary-pos">POS Systems for Maine Dispensaries</a> guide.</p>
    </Callout>

    <section>
      <h2>What This Comparison Covers — and What It Does Not</h2>
      <p>Every vendor below integrates with Maine's Metrc seed-to-sale system (the only state-mandated tracking system). All seven are reputable platforms with paying customers. The differences that matter for a Maine operator are:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pricing transparency.</strong> Of seven vendors, only one (Cova) publishes a starting monthly price on its own site. The other six are quote-only — meaning the "starting at $X" figures that appear on third-party listing sites (Software Advice, G2, SelectHub) reflect estimated typical spend, not vendor list price. We treat those as quote-only.</li>
        <li><strong>Metrc integration depth.</strong> All seven claim native (direct-API) Metrc integration. The operational differentiators are number of supported state markets and Metrc Connect endpoint coverage, not "native vs. not."</li>
        <li><strong>Ecommerce packaging.</strong> Whether online ordering is bundled into the POS subscription or sold as a separate add-on materially changes the all-in monthly cost.</li>
        <li><strong>Public partner economics.</strong> Only one vendor (Flowhub) publishes a referral payout figure. The others compensate via private commission or unpriced partner programs.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This comparison does <strong>not</strong> rank vendors as "best ecommerce" or "best delivery tooling." No Gartner, Forrester, Whitney Economics, BDSA, or NCIA-published comparative analysis of cannabis POS platforms was located in our research. G2 and Capterra are the only non-vendor user-review aggregators with public scores; we link those for each vendor where available. Any "best-in-class" claim beyond those scores is editorial opinion, not third-party analysis.</p>
    </section>

